raspdash
========

A full-screen terminal dashboard for a Raspberry Pi.  It shows:

  1. Machines   -- load, memory and temperatures of the computers on the LAN
  2. Network    -- devices on the LAN and the services they offer
  3. Tasks      -- Google Tasks lists (read-only)
  4. Timetable  -- this week's classes from ruz.spbstu.ru
  5. Weather    -- forecasts from MET Norway for configured cities
  6-8. Markets  -- month and half-year candlestick charts (XAUT/USDT, TON/USDT;
                   BTC/USD, USD/RUB) and a comparison chart

Building from a git checkout:

  ./bootstrap
  ./configure
  make
  make check

A C++23 compiler (GCC 14 or later) is required, plus ncursesw, libcurl,
OpenSSL's libcrypto and nlohmann-json.  See INSTALL for generic
instructions and the Texinfo manual (doc/raspdash.texi, 'info raspdash'
once installed) for configuration and deployment on the Pi.

Configuration: copy config.example.toml to config.toml and edit it.
config.toml and everything in secrets/ are personal and ignored by git.

Enable the formatting hook once per clone:

  git config core.hooksPath hooks

